in categories (e.g., retraining, repairs) might yield different risk levels.\\n\\ndf[\'purpose_encoded\'] = df[\'purpose\'].map({\'radio/tv\': 1, \'new car\': 2, \'used car\': 3, \'education\': 4, \'business\': 5, \'furniture/equipment\': 6, \'other\': 7, \'repairs\': 8, \'domestic appliance\': 9, \'retraining\': 10})\\ndf[\'credit_purpose_risk\'] = df[\'credit_amount\'] * df[\'purpose_encoded\']", "# delayed_flag\\n# Feature description: Binary flag where credit_history is delayed previously, indicating risky past behavior.\\n# Usefulness: Taking delayed payments into account directly reflects past credit reliability.\\n\\ndf[\'delayed_flag\'] = (df[\'credit_history\'] == \'delayed previously\').astype(int)", "# residence_duration_flag\\n# Feature description: Binary flag for individuals with residence_since below the mean value of 2.8. Low residence duration can be indicative of lower stability.\\n# Usefulness: Helps estimate residential stability, which is linked to financial commitment and ability to repay long-term credit.\\n\\ndf[\'residence_duration_flag\'] = (df[\'residence_since\'] < 3).astype(int)", "df.drop(columns=[\'checking_status_encoded\', \'savings_status_encoded\', \'employment_encoded\', \'purpose_encoded\'], inplace=True)"]': 0.025000000000000022}]
