   - Some purposes like education or furniture may pose different levels of risk depending on their interaction with the loan size.

5. Repayment Capacity (installment_commitment): Percentage of income dedicated to repayments.
   - Higher values might indicate strain on disposable income.

6. Stability (residence_duration_flag & residence_since): Residential duration indicates long-term stability.
   - Shorter durations (<3 years) suggest higher instability.

7. Combined Risk Indicators (risk_liquidity_interaction): Interaction of liquidity and delayed payment history.
   - Highlights compounded risks of poor liquidity and past delays.

